{
  "_doc": "The Kelvane Institute line's hull detail (mockup 23, version 5; OpenSpec change kelvane-ship-concepts): what tools/blender/hull_detail.py builds over each class's low-poly hull before painted_bake.py --faction kelvane --ship bakes it onto the ship's own UVs (Ship Design Bible chapters 14 and 15; the ship-detailing skill). Ship space: +x port, +y up, +z bow, metres. A feature off the centreline is mirrored to starboard; nothing repeats. face: where it sits, found by a ray (top: from above at [x, z]; bottom: from below at [x, z]; port: from the port side at [z, y]). The Institute's design language, from its console (kelvane-battle-console D1-D4) and the Calibrators' 'true faces': calibrated plating (cuts 'grid'), enamelled champagne plates pillowed at their edges, dark smoked glass, amber light, a measuring scale engraved down each flank, sensor domes of smoked glass, smooth round pods sunk into the plating, the KID logo; no greebles, trenches or slatted vents (owner, 2026-11-06: 'Mind the clean and sterile and almost scientific aesthetics. They would have decorated their ships with smooth round pieces rather than industrial greebles'). Owner, 2026-11-06: 'start detailing these', 'theme them after advanced science and research vessels, this faction will specialize in scientific missions'.",
